          "open_space_designation": "Local Open Spaces",
          "description": "The playground, within the ownership of the London Borough of Richmond upon Thames, extends to approximately 2,092 m². The extent of encroachment by the Garden Studio proposal is limited to approximately 52 m² or approximately 2.48% of the total operational demise of the play area, representing a minor proportion of the overall area. \nAs both areas are under unified council ownership, the proposal should be considered in the context of a coordinated approach to the management and enhancement of publicly accessible recreational facilities.\nIt is acknowledged that some existing play equipment may require relocation or (subject to warranty) replacement as a consequence of the development. The repositioning and detailed, specification and spatial arrangement of playground and outdoor gym equipment fall outside the scope of this application and will be managed separately by the Council’s Parks and Open Spaces service.\nThe proposal has nevertheless been designed to minimise encroachment and retain the functional use and character of the playground.\n",
